'''''Urtica membranacea''''' is a species of annual herb in the family [[Urticaceae]] native to the [[Mediterranean Basin]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Urtica membranacea |url=http://www.floraiberica.es/floraiberica/texto/pdfs/03_064_01_Urtica.pdf |publisher=[[Flora Iberica]] |access-date=15 April 2022 |page=267}}</ref> They have a self-supporting growth form and simple, broad leaves. Individuals can grow to 39&nbsp;cm tall.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Urtica membranacea Poir. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/5723338|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Urtica membranacea |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/URTI/Urtica_membranacea.php |website=Malta Wild Plants}}</ref>

